    inducingMechanisms: ["An undetected outer-tube-to-tubesheet weld failure combined with an undetected inner-tube-to-tubesheet weld failure lets steam/water reach secondary sodium in the intersheet airspace.", "A through-wall duplex-tube leak injects high-pressure steam/water into liquid sodium, producing heat, hydrogen, sodium compounds and an initial spike-shaped pressure pulse.", "Self-wastage of the failed tube plus target and multi-wastage of adjacent tubes enlarges the leak past the critical size, driving the quasi-steady reaction phase.", "Overheating-type failure of nearby tubes once the reaction-zone temperature climbs opens a larger failure area than wastage alone.", "Backflow of water and reaction products through the superheater relief path that passes through the IHX corrodes or stress-corrosion-cracks the IHX or degrades its heat transfer (IE-19).", "A rapid double-ended guillotine of multiple tubes generates an acoustic/pressure wave that loads the IHX before the shell or secondary piping can relieve.", "Operator failure to dump secondary sodium and water and to scram before IHX failure allows progression to core/structural damage."],
    inducedInitiatorIds: ["IE-05", "IE-06", "IE-17", "IE-18", "IE-19"],
    potentialCombinations: ["Sodium-water reaction over-pressure failing the IHX tubes (IE-19), becoming a primary-to-secondary leak with loss of heat sink (IE-05) and a containment-bypass path.", "Sodium-water reaction with operator failure to scram or dump before IHX failure (operator-error compounded).", "Reaction-generated hydrogen deflagrating in the cover-gas or expansion-tank space.", "Secondary-boundary failure releasing sodium to air, feeding both a fire and the IHX challenge.", "IHX failure leading to primary-coolant-channel or control-rod-driveline plugging (delayed core damage)."],
