    screeningStatus: ScreeningStatus.SCREENED_OUT,
    screeningBasis: "The steam-generator sodium-water reaction is carried as its own special initiating-event category (EVTR/SHTR/SGTR) and screened to a dedicated sodium-water-reaction hazard element rather than folded into ordinary transients, because its phenomenology (pressure spike, quasi-steady reaction, self-wastage propagation, hydrogen and IHX pressure/corrosion loading) is distinct from a normal loss-of-heat-sink transient and is quantified subjectively from physical arguments rather than from EBR-II operating data (no sodium-water reaction occurred at EBR-II owing to the conservative double-walled duplex-tube design requiring breach of two welds). GIF likewise treats it as a dedicated design-basis-leak / containment-bypass topic with its own propagation and pressure-loading evaluation. Its retained initiating forms remain in the internal-events model as IE-17/IE-18 (steam-generator tube leak/rupture) and IE-19 (IHX primary-to-secondary leak).",
