    hazardType: "INTERNAL",
    subcategory: "High-energy line break, pipe whip, jet impingement and internal missiles",
    severityLevels: ["Level 1 - low-stress sodium leak/break bounded by a single pump seizure (inlet) or a loss of primary heat sink (outlet); minimal whip/jet because the primary system runs near atmospheric pressure with a small thermal gradient.", "Level 2 - secondary-sodium or NaK line break with localized jet impingement and a sodium-fire or steam-release source, requiring scram and a secondary dump.", "Level 3 - high-energy steam/feedwater double-ended break with pipe whip and fragment missiles in the steam-generator bay, plus overcooling/loss-of-heat-sink effects.", "Level 4 - catastrophic guillotine break or a missile challenging the primary-tank cover, cover-gas boundary or shutdown-cooler piping, coupling pipe failure to a direct core challenge."],
    affectedAreas: ["Primary-sodium inlet/outlet (Z-pipe) piping in the primary-tank region", "Secondary-sodium piping to and from the IHX within containment", "Steam, feedwater and main-steam piping in the steam-generator bay", "NaK shutdown-cooler piping and air-heat-exchanger boxes", "Cover-gas / expansion-tank lines and reactor-building penetrations"],
