    subcategory: "Heavy-load and fuel/source-handling drop (mechanical impact and fuel-handling reactivity)",
    severityLevels: ["Level 1 - load drop away from the core, sodium boundary and cover that damages only non-safety equipment.", "Level 2 - subassembly drop damaging at most one driver or experiment assembly, bounded by the Potential-Experiment-Damage class (driver-fuel damage precluded).", "Level 3 - fuel-handling reactivity/criticality challenge: a mispositioning or loading error during unrestricted fuel handling trends the subcritical core toward criticality, requiring count-rate trips and operator termination.", "Level 4 - heavy-load impact breaching or distorting the primary-tank cover, support hangers or cover-gas boundary, challenging reactivity control, decay-heat removal, or the sodium/cover-gas boundary."],
    affectedAreas: ["Reactor core grid and individual fuel/experiment subassemblies", "Primary-tank cover, the six radial hanger beams, rotating plugs and gripper/holddown shafts", "Cover-gas boundary, nozzles and instrument-thimble penetrations through the cover", "Fuel-handling-machine area, argon cell and transfer/storage stations", "Local AC and I&C beneath crane load paths"],
