    inducingMechanisms: ["A dropped fuel or experiment subassembly during fuel handling mechanically damages a core assembly or its coolant channel (IE-24, IE-25, IE-26 analogues).", "A loading error or mispositioned high-worth assembly during unrestricted fuel handling inserts positive reactivity and trends the subcritical core toward criticality (IE-29).", "A heavy load handled over the open reactor during an outage is dropped onto the primary-tank cover, support hangers or rotating plugs, distorting the cover or its sodium/cover-gas seals.", "A drop or impact breaches a cover-gas-boundary nozzle or instrument thimble, perturbing primary-tank pressure control and the inert blanket (IE-16).", "Failure of the holddown fingers/gripper or a transfer-device control during handling drops or mis-seats an assembly; loss and re-establishment of hydraulic holddown produces a reactivity step.", "A dropped load damages decay-heat-related penetrations (shutdown-cooler nozzles, shield cooling) on the cover (IE-21)."],
    inducedInitiatorIds: ["IE-16", "IE-21", "IE-24", "IE-25", "IE-26", "IE-29"],
