      "Initiating events were identified by a forward search that combined deductive and inductive methods. A master logic diagram decomposed an uncontrolled radionuclide release through the four SFR safety functions down to the events that challenge each one. Heat-balance fault trees traced the primary-sodium energy balance to the imbalances that defeat heat removal. A failure modes and effects analysis swept every front-line and support system to the component level following the EBR-II system notebooks. An operating-experience review of the EBR-II record and a generic SFR initiator catalogue were screened for events the deductive models might miss. Each candidate was then tested against the plant operating states and the radioactive source inventory carried in the SFR POS workbook.",
